    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91675" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῠρῐ-γενής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,=
		foreg., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>born in</i> or
				<i>from fire</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δράκων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					943
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διόνυσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					13.4.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of
			instruments, <i>wrought</i> or <i>forged by fire</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					1223
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώθων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Henioch.
					1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. παλάμα</span>, i.e. a weapon,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				820
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
